 {"complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-04T15:23:08.617291Z", "id": "RELEASE-007", "priority": "P1", "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-04 on the published v1.1.0 wheel (sha256 f50fff23) in a fresh python3.14 venv: pip install --no-deps rc=0, dist metadata version 1.1.0 correct, but top_level.txt lists __init__, core, dashboard, db, debug_screen, env_service, game_loop, main, memory_reader, observability, ptp_cli, schemas, simple_test, test_all_roms, test_pyboy, vision — i.e. the contents of src/ were installed at site-packages ROOT instead of under a src/ package. Consequences: import src fails (importlib.util.find_spec(\"src\") is None) so every documented AGENTS.md invocation of the form python -m src.game_loop fails from an installed wheel; no entry_points.txt / console script is declared; site-packages is polluted with a bare __init__.py plus generic names (core, main, db) that can collide with other distributions. Root cause: pyproject.toml declares [project] name/version but no [tool.setuptools] package-dir/packages mapping, while the code lives in src/. The sdist keeps the correct src/ layout. Same shape shipped in v1.0.0 (asset ptp_01x_pokemon_ai-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl), so this is a carried-forward artifact gap, recorded in the v1.1.0 release notes Known issues and not a regression of this cut. Publishing nothing: closing this row requires a packaging change plus a rebuilt artifact, which is foreman work.", "status": "complete", "title": "P1 — published wheel is not a usable package: src/* flattened into site-packages root, no entry point, documented 'python -m src.game_loop' fails from the installed artifact (affects v1.0.0 and v1.1.0)", "acceptance_criteria": "1) pyproject.toml declares an explicit setuptools package mapping for the src/ tree ([tool.setuptools] package-dir plus packages, or equivalent), and a fresh python -m build from the tagged tree produces a wheel whose file list has NO module or package at site-packages root other than the real distri