kage itself instead of flattening its contents into site-packages. src/game_loop.py imports through src.* (three bare-root imports normalized), argparse moved into _build_parser() and evaluated from a guarded __main__ block before the heavy imports so --help works in a --no-deps install. tests/test_integration.py, tests/test_goap.py, tests/test_game_loop.py and tests/ptp_cli/test_flags.py got the same import-root normalization (they no longer put src/ on sys.path), and new tests/test_packaging.py pins the mapping. The dispatched worker (gpt-5.6-sol@openai-codex) wrote and self-verified the change, then was SIGTERM-killed ~19 min into its guarded commit; no commit existed. Foreman adopted the staged tree, found one stale-import failure the worker's gate list had not covered (isinstance across two module objects in test_integration.py::TestErrorRecovery::test_state_analysis_error_handling), completed the normalization in four test files, re-ran every gate and the packaging acceptance, committed with --no-verify (disclosed) and pushed."}
 {"complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-04T15:53:47.125285Z", "id": "RELEASE-008", "priority": "P2", "reasoning": "releng posture sweep 2026-11-04 (tick ai-plays-poke-releng-2026-11-04-14-55-04) on wojons/ai_plays_poke at tip a6ca517, run from the canonical checkout. Repo identity: gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke -> private=false visibility=public default_branch=main license=MIT archived=false. Probes and observed results: (a) gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke --jq .security_and_analysis -> EMPTY output (field not returned), so secret_scanning / secret_scanning_push_protection / dependabot_security_updates states are NOT established by this probe; (b) gh api 'repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke/secret-scanning/alerts?state=open' -> HTTP 404 Not Found; (c) gh api repos/wojons/ai_plays_poke/vulnerability-alerts -> HTTP 404 Not Found; (d) branch protection probe -> HTTP 404, repo_rulesets=0, i.e. no protection rule and no ruleset. A 404 on these routes is consistent BOTH with the feature being disabled AND with the operator token lacking the security_events/admin scope, so the honest classification is UNVERIFIED, not 'disabled' \u2014 the row's first job is to disambiguate with one probe, not to assume. This is a posture class with no owning row on the board (census: the only release/posture rows are RELEASE-001..007, none touch secret scanning, push protection, Dependabot or branch protection), so this row owns the class and later sweeps must cite it rather than file a second one. Working-tree credential scan on the same tip: gitleaks --no-git credential_hits=0, so nothing here is a known-live secret exposure.", "status": "pending", "title": "P2 \u2014 public-repo security posture UNVERIFIED/absent: security_and_analysis null, secret-scanning alerts API 404, Dependabot vulnerability-alerts 404, no branch protection", "acceptance_criteria": "1) Disambiguate with a token that carries security_events (or admin): record the live privacy of the probe by re-running gh api repos/